  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_5b2d66bac9db47d9a0ab8c260f96bcf9",
      "statement": "EdgeOne requires the Makers-Conversation-Id header on every agents/* call (missing or malformed → 400), while Feishu's event push is initiated by Feishu's servers and cannot be given a custom header; this is the hard constraint that forces the two-stage architecture (a forwarding layer plus the agent route) and prevents agents/feishu from being the Feishu callback URL directly.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://agents/feishu/index.ts#L3-L14",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:40405e1582e4f56ff78ebda0ac81f058c96cc030c9a426866a02f89e18db53a5:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://cloud-functions/feishu-webhook/index.ts#L21-L25",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c96fdb82ba9e4a8cb201c290376a6fee24f4cc12a44c2f18ea28a23c591a82d9:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/01-%E6%9E%B6%E6%9E%84%E4%B8%8E%E7%A7%BB%E6%A4%8D%E6%98%A0%E5%B0%84.md#L40-L56",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:72921cd4e002c3a72461b027482b38881148c45b6326398e28caf62db58667df:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_439606f764a54bea933dfd8a1c82fdf9",
      "statement": "The conversation id is computed deterministically as `fs-` + the first 32 hex characters of SHA-256(chatId), yielding a constant 35 characters; the naive port `fs-${chatId}` would be 38 characters because a real Feishu chat_id is `oc_` plus 32 hex characters (35), exceeding the platform's 6–36 character limit and allowed charset `0-9 a-z A-Z - _ .`, which fails with 400 for every real conversation while short local test ids pass.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://cloud-functions/feishu-webhook/index.ts#L51-L71",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:476a1d0ac87e4e139550394bf1ca539e7d6a75b3e3397aa2f3468e14fa5fac8a:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/01-%E6%9E%B6%E6%9E%84%E4%B8%8E%E7%A7%BB%E6%A4%8D%E6%98%A0%E5%B0%84.md#L58-L77",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:710e4df7c6ecd7ee7e2bc5937d68a9ffcb576afda8187ce38fafef367017ae4c:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://test/smoke.ts#L505-L518",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9fa1755acff2e0f000f7f25de4677098480bcf6816dc3a0b51323703ef779867:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_842e5dccf48e40219310056e1f015347",
      "statement": "The chat_id→conversation_id hash must remain deterministic because the platform binds sticky routing, store namespace ownership and sandbox instance ownership to the conversation id; a random or time-varying id would break all three (memory and sandbox mix across sessions). The platform also exposes context.store.state as a JSON KV scoped per conversation_id, whose physical keys are state/<conversation_id>/<key>.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://agents/feishu/index.ts#L31-L35",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c833bfa978b82626c8a75d52a4da3621af2c0feeefcf34702126c3e208d26be2:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://cloud-functions/feishu-webhook/index.ts#L62-L64",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f411d46ee6abe0941c833857c98b9d1f5e3e1c23cc9be1654c3a4c312aa4e94b:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/01-%E6%9E%B6%E6%9E%84%E4%B8%8E%E7%A7%BB%E6%A4%8D%E6%98%A0%E5%B0%84.md#L76-L77",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:03fe545d2d9f910423a7a88786b8512dac202b4c29af91bb999c277e3bfa2ddd:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/feishu/store.ts#L7-L11",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a0c4b4846212e1f431e07a33eb31f9fc3e3aba1262224493262b3e2ed460a2b6:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_8d6821c905504decaff6d09e39797825",
      "statement": "The same conversation-id algorithm is duplicated in several independent implementations — cloud-functions/feishu-webhook/index.ts, bridge/index.mjs, the external CF Worker relay src/feishu/edgeone-relay.ts in the cf-agent-lab repository, and the verification scripts tools/ask-bot.mjs and tools/verify-memory.mjs — so changing it without syncing all copies produces the hardest-to-diagnose symptom: cross-session memory bleed or one group landing on different instances. src/feishu/oauth.ts deliberately stores only chatId in the signed OAuth state and lets the forwarding layer compute the id, rather than duplicating the computed value.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://bridge/index.mjs#L51-L59",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:cf42520008590c89951770ea12389660c5f87ca6a67ae65108bfb7975aba45f0:"
        },
