    {
      "id": "claim_f73925051daf4db19d3e909643e4919d",
      "statement": "Three interchangeable ingress implementations exist and must all produce the same conversation id and the same forwarded event fields: the stateless cloud-functions/feishu-webhook (Feishu webhook push, since a cloud function's internal fetch to its own project's agents route is rejected by the platform), the local bridge/index.mjs long-connection process (currently deprecated but kept as a fallback), and the external CF Worker relay at agent.yujizi.org which is the currently active path (v3). The shared contract is: identical hashing, Makers-Conversation-Id header, x-internal-token, body fields messageId/chatId/chatType/openId/text, sender_type=app self-loop filtering, and text-only extraction.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://bridge/index.mjs#L3-L22",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5e7ecad272e18bd89876a34c7847cca0bad0a52eb1b6011ce5dd8889ff19bf83:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://bridge/index.mjs#L70-L89",
