    {
      "id": "claim_c9a8e5c65b0141428ae292c577df875f",
      "statement": "End-to-end verification treats the request header, not chat_id, as the session key: tools/verify-memory.mjs derives four different conversation ids from one real chat_id and asserts they are mutually distinct, which is what proves that session identity is Makers-Conversation-Id; tools/ask-bot.mjs and verify-autocompact.mjs use a fake chat_id with an independent conversation id and read replies from the ?mode=sync HTTP response, so verification never sends a message into a real human chat.",
