    {
      "id": "claim_d65825255ac545dc8c3c38a2765230c2",
      "statement": "The dedupe/rate-limit store is only correct while a single instance handles a given conversation at a time, which the platform's sticky routing provides; it is not a distributed lock, so if one conversation_id is ever routed to two instances dedupe fails and the same message is answered twice. Restoring a stronger guarantee means swapping StateKv (3 methods: get/set/delete) for an external MySQL/PG with a unique(message_id) index.",
      "evidence": [
